# Mandatory self-review before completing work

Before declaring any code change complete, you MUST:

1. Read `AGENTS.md` and review every rule against your changes
2. Specifically verify:
   - **No raw DB access in tests** — all database operations go through `PostgresInteractor`
   - **Assert full objects** — never assert partial responses (single fields, lengths, filtered projections)
   - **No re-fetching known values** — don't SELECT values the caller already has; add them in Python
   - **No `time.sleep`** — never add sleep calls anywhere
   - **No enumerated variables** — use lists, not `x1`, `x2`
3. Only after confirming compliance with ALL rules, report the work as done

If any rule is violated, fix it before reporting completion. Do not rely on `just check-all` alone — it checks tooling (lint, types, coverage) but NOT AGENTS.md conventions.
